{title: 646 - To the Name That Brings Salvation}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #646 • ST. LEONARD • 8.7.8.8.8.7}
{lyricist: Late 15th century}
{composer: Johann Christoph Bach}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 646}
{meta: tune ST. LEONARD}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.8.8.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]To the name [Bb/F]that [Dm]brings [Gm/Bb]salvation
[Gm]Let [C]the [Dm]nations [Bb]bow [C7]the head;
[F]Let them kneel [Bb/F]in [Dm]adoration
[Gm]When [C]this [Dm]name [F/A]of [Bb]names [C7]is said;
[F]Let them pray for [C/E]restoration
[Bb]Of [C]all [C7]things [Dm]in [Am]Christ [C7]the head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]He through every [Dm]generation
[Gm]Rules [Dm]in [F/A]endless [Bb]majesty;
[F]May the kings [Bb/F]of [C/E]every nation
[Gm]Now [C]foreswear [Bb]their enmity,
[F]And with humble [C/E]veneration
[Bb]In [C]the [C7]love [Dm]of [Am]God [C7]agree.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Lord, we pray [Bb/F]for [Dm]upright [C]rulers:
[Gm]Guard [C]them [Dm]surely [Bb]in [C7]their need
[F]From the vanity [Gm/Bb]of [C]power
[Gm]And [C]the [Dm]emptiness [C7]of greed;
[F]Let them see the [C/E]truth [Dm]of [Gm]lowness,
[Bb]And [C]on [C7]justice [Am]let [C7]them feed.
{end_of_verse}
